From: Ahnaf Shahriar <ahnaf.shahriar@neuralink.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] STM32F7_USART: Re-pulse DMA request when bytes remain after
 RDR read

The ReceiveDmaRequest GPIO is pulsed once when BufferState transitions
from Empty to Ready (first byte received).  If additional bytes arrive
before the DMA reads the first, the BufferState setter early-returns
(already Ready) and the DMA request is never re-asserted.

The DMA model transfers one data unit per trigger in peripheral-to-
memory mode.  Without re-pulsing, only the first byte of a multi-byte
frame is DMA-transferred; the remaining bytes sit in the USART queue
and HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback never fires.

After the DMA reads a byte via the RDR register, this patch checks if
more bytes remain in the queue and, if DMA receive is enabled, toggles
ReceiveDmaRequest low then high to trigger the next single-byte DMA
transfer.  The recursion is naturally bounded by the queue depth and
the DMA's data count register.

---
 .../Peripherals/UART/STM32F7_USART.cs        | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/UART/STM32F7_USART.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/UART/STM32F7_USART.cs
index d069f5837..b6f62aed9 100644
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/UART/STM32F7_USART.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/UART/STM32F7_USART.cs
@@ -387,6 +387,11 @@ private uint HandleReceiveData()
             {
                 this.Log(LogLevel.Warning, "No characters in queue.");
             }
+            if(Count > 0 && receiveDmaEnabled.Value)
+            {
+                ReceiveDmaRequest.Set(false);
+                ReceiveDmaRequest.Set(true);
+            }
             return result;
         }
 
